/* Animated cyberpunk HUD for the lock decoration. Display only; no input.
 *
 * The static frame of every widget comes from background.png (generated by
 * render-cyberpunk.py, which reads the HUD_* geometry below). Only the moving
 * parts are drawn here, each inside its own small region.
 *
 * Rendering is client-side: every region owns a small image buffer seeded
 * from the decoded artwork, Cairo/pixman draws the frame on the CPU and the
 * finished pixels go to the background pixmap with one MIT-SHM (or plain)
 * PutImage. The X server therefore only uploads pixels; it never rasterises
 * anti-aliased paths or gradients, which glamor would do through slow
 * software fallbacks. Widgets repaint only when due: smooth motion at ~30 fps,
 * slow readouts at ~15 fps, the memory trace only when its content changes.
 * Nothing touches the SKYNET emblem, the authentication window, the live
 * controls or the power buttons.
 *
 * Defining HUD_NO_X11 leaves out the X11 regions, buffers and property I/O;
 * the widgets, layout, sampling and easing stay. The GTK login screen uses
 * that to draw the same panels with its own toolkit.
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
 */
